        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79410781?u=6f23f56e5eaef76fdbd0167681139d9f478418af&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hi, I found some typos in <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Accelerometer\" rel=\"nofollow\">this page</a> that I fixed.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">doesn't have own methods</code> → <code class=\"notranslate\">doesn't have its own methods</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">doesn't have own events</code> → <code class=\"notranslate\">doesn't have its own events</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Making the docs great and free from mistakes.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">None</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">None</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41389",
            "title": "Docs: Fixed a small typo in the Accelerometer API",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-03T21:33:09.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-03T21:32:25.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ImadSaddik",
                "url": "https://github.com/ImadSaddik"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR is part of a series in which I update the Learn area \"Challenge\" articles. In general, they need to be modernized, restructured, and put in better positions in the modules so they are spaced out better and test subjects that have already been covered.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In this PR specifically, I have updated the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/Text_styling/Typesetting_a_homepage\" rel=\"nofollow\">CSS typesetting</a> challenge to improve the styling, modernize the techniques used (for example, it was using floats for multi-column layout), and make it consistent with the other challenge I've recently updated.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41384",
            "title": "Update typesetting challenge",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-03T12:58:37.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-03T12:56:29.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">I have worked on these examples pages often enough to be saddened by their current situation. I'm going to invest some effort in modernizing them; as a first step, I need to weed out everything that's not related to the DOM, such as CSSOM or HTML. The \"examples\" page almost exclusively contains demonstrations of CSSOM and HTML, so they are moved to their respective locations.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Please don't review the exact words written here; I have not written anything. I merely moved things around. I'll rewrite them right next.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41381",
            "title": "Modernize DOM guide (1): update interface list, disband intro/examples pages",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-03T11:56:27.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-03T04:46:48.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Josh-Cena",
