        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #41379.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3479515543\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41379\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41379/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41379\">#41379</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The interesting bit of this is that it finds the stylesheet to use based on the name of the generated output inline style block, which I discovered by inspection. Provided this does not change it is more robust for examples. More important though, it is a better technique for finding a style of interest.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"const stylesheet = document.styleSheets[1];\n// Find the inline stylesheet generated for MDN live samples\nconst stylesheet = document.querySelector(&quot;style#css-output&quot;).sheet;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">stylesheet</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">document</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">styleSheets</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">[</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">]</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-c\">// Find the inline stylesheet generated for MDN live samples</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">stylesheet</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">document</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">querySelector</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s\">\"style#css-output\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">sheet</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">FYI is also possible to search for external stylesheets. We need to document that somewhere too. Something like this.</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"// Find the stylesheet by its href\nconst stylesheet = [...document.styleSheets].find(\n  (s) =&gt; s.href?.includes(&quot;your-styles.css&quot;)\n);\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">// Find the stylesheet by its href\nconst stylesheet = [...document.styleSheets].find(\n  (s) =&gt; s.href?.includes(\"your-styles.css\")\n);\n</code></pre></div>",
