        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This updates the TrustedType documentation for <code class=\"notranslate\">HTMLScriptElement.textContent</code> so that it includes boilerplate and security considerations.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">These was inherited from node but is now in IDL - see <a href=\"https://w3c.github.io/trusted-types/dist/spec/#enforcement-in-scripts\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://w3c.github.io/trusted-types/dist/spec/#enforcement-in-scripts</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note that this essentially copies <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLScriptElement/text\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">HTMLScriptElement.text</code></a> which was updated in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3416594111\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41128\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41128/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41128\">#41128</a>. The only minor difference is the note about the fact it is also defined on Node and so can be used with other elements.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Project tracking in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2770544982\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37518\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/37518/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37518\">#37518</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41341",
            "title": "HTMLScriptElement.textContent/innerText - docs for TrustedTypes",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-04T06:45:17.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-30T07:22:38.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36165315?u=c2fe18f0153b07e496e9fdaa6f6874a7d1eecce2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR fixes the “Ordered list” example on the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/sibling-index?utm_source=chatgpt.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">sibling-index()</a> documentation page.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The bug: The old example set content: var(--list-index); where --list-index was just an integer. The CSS content property does not accept raw numbers, so the pseudo-element would render nothing.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The fix: By introducing a CSS counter (counter-set + counter()), the numeric value from sibling-index() is converted into a valid, displayable string.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #41290.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3452935402\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41290\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41290/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41290\">#41290</a></p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41339",
            "title": "#41290 CSS: Fix sibling-index() example to use counters with content",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-30T04:37:50.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-30T04:12:09.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "sagarp2901",
                "url": "https://github.com/sagarp2901"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12285999?u=183d27a6aca0718cb83ecec3c8e7745502384f48&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h1 dir=\"auto\">Add reference for CSS value serialization, especially colors</h1>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #32734.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2193690629\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/32734\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/32734/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/32734\">#32734</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds a new guide explaining CSS value serialization through JavaScript APIs, with a focus on how color values (hsl(), hwb(), etc.) are serialized to rgb()/rgba() format when accessed via getComputedStyle() or getPropertyValue().</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This documentation helps developers understand why and how CSS values, especially colors, might return in different formats than they were written. This addresses a common source of confusion when working with CSS values through JavaScript APIs.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">References:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom/#serialize-a-css-value\" rel=\"nofollow\">CSSOM Specification - Serializing CSS Values</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-4/#serialization\" rel=\"nofollow\">CSS Color Module Level 4 - Serialization</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #32734.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2193690629\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/32734\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/32734/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/32734\">#32734</a> - Creates documentation for CSS value serialization, especially for colors</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41322",
            "title": "docs: Add reference for CSS value serialization, especially colors",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-29T04:06:11.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-28T23:03:51.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Shrinivassab",
                "url": "https://github.com/Shrinivassab"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105274?u=173310b843e2751843265438af8cfb79eda02039&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Adds <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;form&gt;</code> wrapper and <code class=\"notranslate\">preventDefault</code> handler</li>\n<li>Changes the inline demo and the step-by-step guide to match</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To have a better UX: pressing Enter in the field now adds an item.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Based on the original PR <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3200964178\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40201\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/40201/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40201\">#40201</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3441952460\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/learning-area/issues/820\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/learning-area/pull/820/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/learning-area/pull/820\">mdn/learning-area#820</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><g-emoji class=\"g-emoji\" alias=\"warning\">⚠️</g-emoji> Should be merged together.</p>",
